      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To steelman the pro-border security side, focus on the concepts of national sovereignty and the rule of law as foundational principles of a stable state. Argue that effective border control is a necessary function of any sovereign nation to manage its territory and maintain internal order. Furthermore, you can introduce the argument that robust security measures are not just about stopping illegal immigration, but about managing national security risks, such as potential threats from transnational crime or hostile state actors. These arguments move beyond simple \"stop the illegal crossings\" talking points into sophisticated policy defense.",
